Custom Code-writing style used-:
1) Use the methods for the functionality of widgets in a file named name_of_widgetfile_functionalities.dart
   for the file named widgetfile.dart
   which will have the test file named widgetfile_testnametest.dart.
2) Class names for the functionalities of the widget file will be ClassNameWithTheUIFunctionalities.
3) File name for the functionalities file will be file_name_of_ui_file_functionality.dart
4) Feature first layout for files used in the codebase. All the files related to a feature are stored in a separate folder.
   The details are present in this article. https://codewithandrea.com/articles/flutter-project-structure/
5) In the integration tests, the code practice used will be without grouping where one tester object will keep on testing all the flows.
   To segregate features and make the code more readable, comments will be used to denote feature being tested by the code.
6) Caveats of the architecture used-:
The files counter_event.dart, drop_down_event.dart and inherited_widget_functionality.dart are all kept in shared folder for now as the code is common to game_information and game_parameter feature.
7) Explain new code concepts in the first commit of using them through code comments. Then remove the code comments that explain said public concepts in the very next commit on that branch.
   Tracking of the comments will be done in a file, created in the first commit containing this line in this file, in root directory named comments_to_be_deleted_in_next_commit.
8) When merging two branches, the first commit on the merge should have changes mentioned in this file for the commit message section that will cover what was introduced in the branch having latest changes.
9) Page object model for test code.

